l sorted-key JSON + sha256 pin + price; the generator PROVES the contrast pairs with the same math as ThemePack before writing (the gate re-proves in Java — no coincidence agreement). Gate 15 of the pipeline (ci/theme_store_gate.sh + ThemeStoreGate.java, 112 checks): all 25 packs PASS with hash pins verified, review latency p50 0.096ms (bar 5ms, ~52x headroom), 23 designed harmful packs ALL refused with the right tag, post-review byte flip caught by the pin, full simulated month over the catalog: gross 125,080c, refunds 5,633c, creator 83,609c = 70.00% / platform 35,838c = 30.00% — the ledger closes to the cent. Tests 843 -> 923 (+52 ThemePackTest, +28 EconomyTest; suites now emit the pipeline's RESULT convention). NEGATIVE PROOF: hiding ThemePack.java -> THEME_STORE_GATE_FAILED compile exit 1 (restored, re-verified OK). Environment lesson measured: the recycled sandbox lost javac/tools(android,r8) — JVM gates held via the documented ECJ path, and sync_client_gate gained the run.sh stub fallback (tests/stubs/android/** — compile-time-only types) when tools/android.jar is absent; contract documented in the script. dex unchanged (ThemePack/Economy unreachable from manifest paths -> R8-stripped, zero-byte cost until the store UI week; r8 gate ran where the tools exist). Contract: docs/STORE.md. Full doc: docs/PHASE2-W3-REPORT.md. Next: week 4 = item C (iOS readiness — pure reference NQF reader, golden vectors, Swift spec).
